Description:

JMAP Mailbox/set, Calendar/set, and AddressBook/set now reject a shareWith
entry whose sharee is not a valid userid.  Previously any string was accepted
and later appended to a filesystem path when recording that sharee's
subscriptions, so a sharee holding path separators or traversal components
could cause a file to be written outside the directory intended for it.


CVE number:

(not yet assigned)
Tracked as GitHub security advisory GHSA-3525-275g-p67h.


CVE description:

JMAP sharing permits path traversal through a sharee userid

An authenticated JMAP user could share a mailbox, calendar, or address book
with a sharee that was not a valid userid, and cause the server to write a
file outside the directory intended for it.


